# Copy to .env for local dev (gitignored, loaded automatically by main.go).
# In production (Render), set these as service environment variables instead —
# .env files aren't deployed (see .dockerignore).

# Path to the Stockfish binary. Local dev only — the Docker image sets this
# itself (apt-installed Stockfish at /usr/games/stockfish).
STOCKFISH_PATH=stockfish

# Free personal token from https://lichess.org/account/oauth/token (no scopes
# needed). Powers GET /api/*/explorer; that endpoint 503s without it.
LICHESS_TOKEN=

# Restrict CORS to your deployed frontend's origin in production, e.g.
# https://chesslab-frontend.onrender.com. Defaults to "*" (any origin) if unset.
ALLOWED_ORIGIN=

# --- Auth (required) ---
# The one login gating the whole app (see internal/auth's package doc).
# Seeded into Postgres's `users` table (bcrypt-hashed) at boot — changing
# these and redeploying rotates the password. Without a database configured
# below, the server falls back to comparing against these directly.
AUTH_USERNAME=
AUTH_PASSWORD=
# HMAC signing key for login JWTs. If unset, a random one is generated each
# boot (fine for local dev — it just means restarting logs everyone out);
# set an explicit value in production so tokens survive a redeploy.
# Generate one with: openssl rand -hex 32
JWT_SECRET=

# --- Trainer progress sync + analytics (optional) ---
# Postgres connection string (Neon or any Postgres works) for cross-device
# trainer progress (card_progress table) and drilling analytics
# (line_attempts table, auto-pruned — see LINE_ATTEMPTS_RETENTION_DAYS).
# Without this, the trainer still works, it just won't remember progress
# between sessions/devices, and /api/progress + /api/analytics return 503.
DATABASE_URL=
# How many days of line_attempts to keep before they're pruned (a log for
# analytics/future scheduling tweaks, not core scheduling state — see
# internal/db/schema.sql). Defaults to 90.
# LINE_ATTEMPTS_RETENTION_DAYS=90

# --- Private book PDFs (Backblaze B2) ---
# The reader fetches only the requested chapter object, through the backend.
# Object names are derived as books/<book-id>/chapter-<number>.pdf.
B2_KEY_ID=
B2_APPLICATION_KEY=
B2_BUCKET=
# B2_CHAPTER_PREFIX=books

# --- AI coach (optional) ---
# Not deployed to Render — there's no local LLM there, so the coach endpoints
# (/coach/explain, /coach/chat) just return 503 in production, same as when
# Stockfish is unavailable. Only relevant if you run Ollama yourself somewhere
# reachable from the backend.
OLLAMA_BASE_URL=
COACH_MODEL=

# --- Data paths (rarely need changing) ---
# REPERTOIRES_PATH=data/repertoires
# COACH_CHUNKS_PATH=data/opening-sources/accelerated-dragon/chunks.validated.json
# COACH_OVERVIEW_PATH=data/opening-sources/accelerated-dragon/overview.json
